LOK: Calc formats cells by address

- .uno:ElyStructure's new verb range.format applies cell formats and
  borders to the addressed range as one undo step (one
  ScUndoSelectionAttr carrying the pattern and the frame, as the view's
  ApplyPatternLines records), so the cursor, selection and shown sheet
  stay. Value is key=value lines, already checked by the caller: bold,
  italic, underline, wrap (1 or 0), font, size (twips), color and
  background (decimal RGB or none), number (an en-US format code), align,
  valign, and border-left/top/right/bottom/inner-h/inner-v ("none" or
  "style:width:color", width in twips). Bold, italic, font and size apply
  to Latin, Asian and complex text alike; edges not named keep theirs.
- .uno:StructureAt answers "number" when the format code does not parse,
  and range.format shares the other verbs' refusals (no such sheet,
  protected, address).

